            {
               "text": "### Images from Dons Maps\n\nThese images are copyright for Dons' Maps and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHer\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHer', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Fossil of Homo heidelbergensis. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the Western Australian Museum (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite1>)</li><li>Multiplying with the body (Level 1): In this text, we deepen our knowledge about the evolution of human beings, besides multiplying using our body (<htcite2>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHer1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHer1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Skeleton of <i>Homo ergaster</i>. © Don Hitchcock. Original (<htcite3>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite4>)</li><li>Where Are They?: In this last text of the chapter, we learn where we can find the numbers studied throughout the chapter (<htcite5>).</li><li>Walking and singing - Who was the first person in the family to walk? What is the relationship of that with the indigenous numbers? (<htcite6>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">3 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgFlore\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgFlore', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Fossil of Homo floresiensis on the left. © Don Hitchcock. Original at The Natural History Museum, Cromwell Road, London SW7 5BD (<htcite7>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite8>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">4 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgDon\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgDon', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Venus of Willendorf built around <htdate0>. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the <i>Vienna Natural History Museum</i> (<htcite9>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite10>)</li><li>Wu Family (武): Family of the empress Wu Zetian (武則天) (<htcite11>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">5 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHr0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHr0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\"> Reconstruction of the skull of Homo rudolfensis on the left. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the Vienna Natural History Museum (<htcite12>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite13>)</li><li>The Mutapa State (1450 - 1663): In this text, we study the development of the empire from an external perspective (<htcite14>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">6 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHabilis\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHabilis', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Reconstruction of the skull of Homo habilis. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the Vienna Natural History Museum (<htcite15>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite16>)</li><li>Exercising with numbers - We perform a body exercise with numbers to fix the sum of units and tens (<htcite17>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">7 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgPb\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgPb', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Skull of Paranthropus boisei on the left. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the Vienna Natural History Museum (<htcite18>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite19>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">8 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHe\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHe', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Skull of Homo erectus on the left. © Don Hitchcock. Original at the Vienna Natural History Museum (<htcite20>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite21>).</li><li>Walking and singing - Who was the first person in the family to walk? What is the relationship of that with the indigenous numbers? (<htcite22>).</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">9 / 9</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgNean\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgNean', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\"></div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>  </li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
